To access claims in an ASP.NET Core Web API that is protected using Azure AD B2C, follow these steps:


---

Step 1: Ensure Your API is Configured for Authentication

1. Go to Azure AD B2C → App registrations.


2. Register Your API if not already done.


3. Expose an API:

Under Expose an API, set an Application ID URI (e.g., api://your-api-client-id).

Define Scopes (e.g., user.read).



4. Set Permissions:

In Authentication, make sure your API allows token authentication.

In API permissions, add Microsoft Graph → openid, profile, email.

Click Grant admin consent.





---

Step 2: Secure API with JWT Authentication

Modify appsettings.json:

{
  "AzureAdB2C": {
    "Instance": "https://yourtenant.b2clogin.com",
    "ClientId": "your-api-client-id",
    "Domain": "yourtenant.onmicrosoft.com",
    "SignUpSignInPolicyId": "B2C_1A_signup_signin",
    "Issuer": "https://yourtenant.b2clogin.com/{tenantId}/v2.0/"
  }
}

Update Program.cs:

using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.JwtBearer;
using Microsoft.Identity.Web;

var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);

builder.Services.AddAuthentication(JwtBearerDefaults.AuthenticationScheme)
    .AddMicrosoftIdentityWebApi(builder.Configuration.GetSection("AzureAdB2C"));

builder.Services.AddAuthorization();
builder.Services.AddControllers();

var app = builder.Build();
app.UseAuthentication();
app.UseAuthorization();
app.MapControllers();
app.Run();


